From efafa04af5b43fb5a13acb9f457b60fe17eb4275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0xx <29106114+n-000000@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:21:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Port musictide-patches to v0.170.6
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Re-derive the musictide fork patches (groups A–F) onto upstream v0.170.6,
carried over from the v0.170.5 port via the squashed patch.

v0.170.6 pins @sveltia/ui ^0.42.1, which fixes the raw `_sui.cancel` render
on the file-uploader Cancel button: 0.41.5's initLocales() loaded its own
locale strings via an `import.meta.glob(..., ?raw)` that registered nothing
when the CMS re-bundled the dep, so every `_sui.*` key resolved to its raw
name. 0.42.1 imports the YAML as parsed objects. Proven in the built bundle:
`Previous Decade`/`Next Decade`/`Previous Month` (strings that exist only in
@sveltia/ui locales) go 0 -> 1 occurrences after the bump.

One 3-way conflict resolved: toolbar.svelte's $copyFromLocaleToast keeps our
{#if message} guard on top of 0.170.6's {@const}->{const} syntax switch.

Build clean (901 modules, 2.06 MB); full suite 6901 passed (248 files).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015n5e4iGe4XNnr52fWi6RYP
